ary line asked of each retained chain; a non-round carries none; a combined sitting carries it once after its last section and says where the verdict writes it; and those outcome and stopping-boundary lines do not alter parsed row rulings or judged rows.\""," tier = \"Full\"","-expected = \"Satisfies LLR-360 (parent SR-161): a decomposition-round sitting presents each applicable perspective question and requires one outcome, while another sitting has no perspective question; the minted and in-lane routes reach one perspective set for one system requirement wherever the authoring work item is named; optional-slot, combined-sitting, absent-roster, unreadable-roster, and verdict-parsing outcomes remain as stated.\"","+expected = \"Satisfies LLR-360 (parents SR-161 and SR-186): a decomposition-round sitting presents each applicable perspective question and requires one outcome, while another sitting has no perspective question; the minted and in-lane routes reach one perspective set for one system requirement wherever the authoring work item is named; optional-slot, combined-sitting, absent-roster, unreadable-roster, and verdict-parsing outcomes remain as stated; a decomposition round's sitting brief asks the verdict for each retained chain's stopping reason.\""," automated = \"Yes\"","-evidence = \"tests/test_plan_briefs.py::test_a_sitting_with_no_first_approval_sr_and_no_amended_need_says_it_is_no_decomposition_round; tests/test_plan_briefs.py::test_outside_a_round_the_roster_is_not_read; tests/test_plan_briefs.py::test_an_amended_need_is_a_parent_the_work_items_refs_do_not_reach; tests/test_plan_briefs.py::test_a_judged_sr_reaches_hats_through_the_need_it_names; tests/test_plan_briefs.py::test_the_work_items_tags_widen_each_need_and_sibling_needs_never_merge; tests/test_plan_briefs.py::test_an_absent_roster_yields_the_opt_out_line_in_a_round; tests/test_plan_briefs.py::test_a_malformed_roster_refuses_a_round_naming_the_roster; tests/test_plan_briefs.py::test_the_roun